{"created": "2023-08-26T11:10:39.799693+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-15T06:02:13.817596+00:00", "id": 8060268, "conceptrecid": "8060267", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.8060268", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.8060267", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.8060268", "metadata": {"title": "SPEI-GD: The first global multi-scale daily SPEI dataset for 1983-2020", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.8060268", "publication_date": "2023-06-20", "description": "<p>The global daily SPEI dataset (SEPI-GD) at 0.25&deg; spatial resolution form 1982 to 2021. This depository includes the five files of the daily SPEI data with five time scales (5, 30, 90, 180, and 360 days). The calculation based on ERA5's precipitation and Singer's potential evapotranspiration. All data are geographic latitude-longitude projection and NetCDF format. See paper for detailed explanation: Liu X, Yu S, Yang Z, et al. The first global multi-timescale daily SPEI dataset from 1982 to 2021[J]. Scientific Data, 2024, 11(1): 223.</p>", "access_right": "restricted", "creators": [{"name": "Liu, Xuebang", "affiliation": "Peking University"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "tops"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": false, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "8060267"}}]}}, "title": "SPEI-GD: The first global multi-scale daily SPEI dataset for 1983-2020", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/8060268", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/8060268", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/8060268?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.8060268", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.8060268", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.8060268", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/8060268/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/8060267", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/8060267", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.8060267"